      "notes": "r is the fraction of nodes REMOVED; the boundary set keeps the highest-degree n*(1-r) nodes, one per connected component minimum. Kept nodes are ORIGINAL nodes with their own features and labels, so nothing is aggregated. Reduced edge weights are Schur-complement conductances; on these tree-like citation graphs the reduction is sparser than the original (leaf pruning dominates fill-in). max|L_red @ 1| ~ 1e-14 confirms the reduced matrix is a valid Laplacian, as the paper proves."
